# Vesti Motion and Media
- Motion must clarify state or improve perceived quality.
- Prefer existing CSS transitions and current project capabilities.
- Do not add Framer Motion or another animation library unless explicitly approved.
- Keep animation restrained, fast, and premium.
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion.
- Avoid continuous decorative animation.
- Avoid excessive parallax, glow, bouncing, or floating effects.
- Product and face imagery must remain visually stable.
- Optimize media with appropriate sizing and lazy loading where relevant.
- Do not lower image quality in the main try-on or result experience.
- Before/After interactions must remain smooth and touch-friendly.
- On iPad retail screens, prioritize stable layout and responsive interaction over animation spectacle.
